<Layout title="Research" active="Research" description="Research of Abhishek Karna.">

  <h1>Research</h1>

  <section class="project">
    <h2>Machine learning for quantum materials</h2>
    <p class="entry-meta">Princeton University, 2026 to present. With <a href="https://bernevig-group.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">B. Andrei Bernevig</a>.</p>
    <p>
      I build generative models for crystal structures and models that predict magnetic, superconducting
      and other properties of materials.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="project">
    <h2>Quantum Monte Carlo for lattice Hamiltonians</h2>
    <p class="entry-meta">Duke University, 2024 to 2026. With <a href="https://scholars.duke.edu/person/sch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shailesh Chandrasekharan</a>.</p>
    <p>
      I developed projected density matrix sampling, a continuous-time quantum Monte Carlo method for the
      low-lying spectrum of lattice Hamiltonians, free of Trotter error. We applied it to the Ising chain near
      the E<sub>8</sub> critical point and to the frustrated Shastry&ndash;Sutherland model.
    </p>
    <p class="entry-links">
      <a href="https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/gtbl-vsdt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Physical Review D</a>
      <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.19209" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">arXiv</a>
      <a href="/projects/Hvar2025 - ICSCQM Poster - Karna, Abhishek.pdf" target="_blank">Poster, ICSCQM 2025</a>
      <a href="/pdms-presentation.pdf" target="_blank">Slides, Max Planck Graduate Center 2026</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="project">
    <h2>Synthesis of quantum magnets</h2>
    <p class="entry-meta">Duke University, 2022 to 2026. With <a href="https://scholars.duke.edu/person/Sara.Haravifard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sara Haravifard</a>.</p>
    <p>
      I made the doped spinels Li<sub>x</sub>Zn<sub>1&minus;x</sub>V<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> and
      Cr-doped ZnAl<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> by solid-state reaction and refined their structures from powder
      X-ray diffraction. I arc-melted the borides TmB<sub>4</sub> and HoB<sub>4</sub>, grew single crystals of
      NdFeO<sub>3</sub> in an optical floating-zone furnace, oriented them by Laue diffraction and measured
      their magnetization.
    </p>
    <p class="entry-links">
      <a href="/projects/APS Global Physics Summit - Karna, Abhishek - 2025.pdf" target="_blank">Poster, APS 2025</a>
      <a href="/projects/Spinel + Topological Magnon - Karna, Abhishek - 2024.pdf" target="_blank">Poster, 2024</a>
      <a href="/projects/Spinel_Doping - Karna, Abhishek - 2023.pdf" target="_blank">Poster, 2023</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="project">
    <h2>Air pollution in Nepal</h2>
    <p class="entry-meta">Duke University, 2022 to 2026. With <a href="https://scholars.duke.edu/person/brian.mcadoo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brian McAdoo</a>, <a href="https://planetlab.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlanetLab</a>.</p>
    <p>
      We measured the transport of fine particulate matter across the border into the Terai of Nepal with a
      low-cost sensor network and back-trajectory modeling.
    </p>
    <p class="entry-links">
      <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apr.2026.102920" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atmospheric Pollution Research</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="project">
    <h2>Track reconstruction for the HL-LHC</h2>
    <p class="entry-meta">Duke University, 2023. With Ashutosh Kotwal.</p>
    <p>
      As a Huang Fellow I wrote algorithms that divide the silicon detector into wedges and sort collision hits
      into them, for parallel track reconstruction in the trigger.
    </p>
    <p class="entry-links">
      <a href="/projects/Huang Fellows - HL-LHC Algorithm - Karna, Abhishek - 2023.pdf" target="_blank">Poster</a>
      <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-17888-0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Scientific Reports (acknowledged)</a>
    </p>
  </section>

</Layout>
